 "year": 2020,
 "metric": "LAeq 24h, dBA, 30 m grid; value at the address point (pixel containing it)",
 "threshold_note": "BTS models noise only above ~45 dBA. null = below threshold for that source (quieter), listed in below_threshold. Model ignores barriers, buildings, helicopters, industry and ports. BTS's combined and per-source rasters are offset by about one 30 m pixel from each other in places (also visible in BTS's own map tiles), so at a single point the combined value can be lower than one source; max_50m_db is the more robust indicator next to busy roads/tracks.",
 "max_50m_note": "max_50m_db = highest combined value among 30 m pixels within 50 m of the point (noisiest nearby frontage); max_50m_source = source (road/aviation/rail) with the highest single-source value within the same 50 m.",
 "logan_note": "logan_contour is null: Massport publishes Logan DNL contours only as report maps, no queryable GIS layer was found. Use aviation_db (BTS aviation LAeq) as the proxy.",
 "distance_note": "highway/rail: straight-line metres to the nearest OpenStreetMap way (not in tunnel); highways = ways of the I-93, US 1, Route 2, I-90, Route 16, Route 1A route relations (ramps excluded); rail = railway=rail/light_rail/subway running tracks (sidings, yards, industrial/crane tracks excluded).",
